<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <AnalysisLevel>preview</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisMode>AllEnabledByDefault</AnalysisMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Promptuarium</PackageId>
    <Title>Promptuarium</Title>
    <Description>Promptuarium is a versatile, tree-based data structure to store or exchange data and metadata efficiently (in binary format). Written in pure C#, can be used in F#, too.</Description>
    <PackageTags>promptuarium binary tree serialization space-efficient limitless container</PackageTags>
    <ReleaseNotes>New: Promptuarium.Serializer, a separate, experimental package (opt-in PRMTSER000): .NET objects to trees and back, without JSON, in the layout of SERIALIZER_FORMAT.md (PRMT:GEN1-LE, PRMT:CFG1-LE or a signature of the application), with comments. pedit and PStudio show the metadata before the data. PStudio: only the forms that give a content back byte for byte are offered; the tags and the type codes of the serializer layout by name; the chosen forms are remembered for every file (View / Reset Types forgets them); File / Open Recent; the settings are kept. GetStatistics().ToString() lists the metadata lines first. The library API and the binary format are unchanged.</ReleaseNotes>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>The library, its API and the binary format are unchanged since 8.4.0. Released together with Promptuarium.Serializer 8.4.1, which adds CONTAINER (0xF1) to version 2 of the serializer layout: a nested tree, the raw bytes of a whole Promptuarium stream, stored like a BLOB but checked to be one complete tree. The tools follow it: pcfg checks CONTAINER values, shows them as container:HEX with their size, signature and nodes, sets them with container:HEX or container:file:PATH, and exports them as !container (YAML, imported back byte for byte) or base64 (JSON); PStudio knows the type and opens its value as a nested tree. pedit, pcfg, ppak, ppakz and dump print their version with --version (-V); PStudio shows it in the window title and in Help / About. A file with a CONTAINER is not read by 8.4.0 and earlier (an unknown type code); the other files of version 2 are unchanged.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
